// PARAM: --analysis int
// Adapted from Goblint tests/regression/20-slr_term/03-3ctxs.c (a NOCHECK
// termination test; the post-loop check i == 10 is added). The same
// program under --context entry-state (16-composite-domain/precision/
// 03-3ctxs_parity_bounds_entry_state.vimp) proves it, and inlining f
// proves it in the context-insensitive analysis too, so the composite
// itself has the precision.
//
// Mechanism: f has one context-insensitive FunctionEntry unknown, fed by
// side effect from the call site inside the loop. The head's widening
// makes the call site deliver a growing i, and the entry unknown widens
// against it to the i32 limit. j + 1 may then overflow, so under the
// default assume_top f returns the full i32 range, and 1 + t may overflow
// as well. Side-effected unknowns only ever grow, so the caller's narrowing
// never reaches f's entry (measured with --graph-snapshot: entry_f j and
// the call site's t are the full i32 range, the loop body's i is
// [-2147483648,9]). After the loop the exit guard leaves i =
// [10,2147483647] with congruence top: nothing singles out 10. Distinct
// from 03-procedures/known-imprecision/01-two_call_sites_same_procedure.vimp,
// which merges two call sites; here a single call site loses to widening on the entry
// unknown that the caller's own narrowing never reaches.
fun i32 f(i32 j) {
  return j + 1;
}
fun main() {
  i32 i = 0;
  while (i < 10) {
    i32 t = f(i);
    i = 1 + t;
  }
  __voblint_check(i == 10); // UNKNOWN
}
